                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/toposes"} toposes
              is to pass to
              %em parameterized
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-category"} 0-categories
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
              categories. Although these
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topoi
              behave much like the 1-topos
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spaces"} spaces
              that may carry more structure. For instance, a (pre)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+smooth+space"} generalized smooth space
          %p
