          %h3#syntax_in_univalent_homotopy_type_theory Syntax in univalent homotopy type theory
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            \-Toposes provide
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence"} univalent
            Tarskian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+of+types"} type of types
            (which inteprets as the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object+classifier"} object classifier
          %p For more on this see at
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/homotopytypetheory/show/model+of+type+theory+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} model of type theory in an (infinity,1)-topos
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "relation+between+type+theory+and+category+theory#HomotopyWithUnivalence"} relation between type theory and category theory – Univalent homotopy type theory and infinity-toposes
          %h2#ToposTheory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            \-Topos theory
          %p
            Most of the standard constructions in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+theory"} topos theory
            have or should have immediate generalizations to the context of
            = succeed "-toposes," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            exist for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-categories
          %p For instance there are evident notions of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"}> geometric morphism
              s between
              = succeed "-toposes," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+section"} global section
              geometric morphism to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-sheaf
              = succeed "-topos" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
          %p
            Moreover, it turns out that
            = succeed "-toposes" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
