          %p and with an intrinsic notion of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"}> homotopy in an (∞,1)-topos
              \.
          %p
            In classical topos theory, cohomology and homotopy of a topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            are defined in terms of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial object
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
