          %p
            In retrospect, at least the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} homotopy categories
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} (∞,1)-toposes
            have been known since
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kenneth+Brown"}> Kenneth Brown
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BrownAHT"} Abstract homotopy theory and generalized sheaf cohomology
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "http://www.jstor.org/stable/1996573"} jstor:1996573
          %p
            presented there via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+of+fibrant+objects"} categories of fibrant objects
            among
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaves"} simplicial presheaves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} of simplicial presheaves
            originates wit:h
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"}> André Joyal
                , Letter to
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Grothendieck"} Alexander Grothendieck
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "http://webusers.imj-prg.fr/~georges.maltsiniotis/ps/lettreJoyal.pdf"} pdf scan
            %li#JardineLecture
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+F.+Jardine"}> John F. Jardine
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Simplicial presheaves
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://core.ac.uk/download/pdf/82485559.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            A more intrinsic characterization of these “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+toposes"}> model toposes
            ” (
            %a{:href => "#Rezk10"}> Rezk 2010
            ) as
            = succeed "-toposes" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Simpson99"} Simpson 1999
          %ul
            %li#Simpson99
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Carlos+Simpson"}> Carlos Simpson
              ,
              %em
                A Giraud-type characterization of the simplicial categories associated to closed model categories as
                = succeed "-pretopoi" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9903167"}> arXiv:math/9903167
              )
          %p
            The generalization of these
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+toposes"} model toposes
            from 1-sites to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+site"} simplicial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+sites"} model sites
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#ToenVezzosi05
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bertrand+To%C3%ABn"}> Bertrand Toën
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gabriele+Vezzosi"} Gabriele Vezzosi
              = succeed "," do
                %em Homotopical Algebraic Geometry I: Topos theory
              %strong 193
              2 (2005) 257-372 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.AG/0207028"}> arXiv:math.AG/0207028
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.aim.2004.05.004"} doi:10.1016/j.aim.2004.05.004
          %p
            The term
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              \-topos
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#Lurie03
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                On
                = succeed "-Topoi" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0306109"}> arXiv:math/0306109
              )
          %p
            The term
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+topos"} model topos
            was later coined in:
          %ul
            %li#Rezk10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Rezk"}> Charles Rezk
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Toposes and homotopy toposes
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://rezk.web.illinois.edu/homotopy-topos-sketch.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Rezk_HomotopyToposes.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            A comprehensive conceptualization and discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} (∞,1)-toposes
            is then due to
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              , section 6.1 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} Higher Topos Theory
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 170
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://press.princeton.edu/titles/8957.html"} pup:8957
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.math.ias.edu/~lurie/papers/HTT.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            building on
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Rezk10"} Rezk 2010
            = succeed "-stack" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "-toposes." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/models+for+%E2%88%9E-stack+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} models for ∞-stack (∞,1)-toposes
          %p Overview:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis-Charles+Cisinski"}> Denis-Charles Cisinski
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Catégories supérieures et théorie des topos
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.univ-toulouse.fr/~dcisinsk/1097.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Rezk19
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Rezk"}> Charles Rezk
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lectures on Higher Topos Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://rezk.web.illinois.edu/leeds-lectures-2019.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/RezkHigherToposTheory2019.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            A useful collection of facts of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+homotopy+theory"} simplicial homotopy theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-topos+theory"} (infinity,1)-topos theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zhen+Lin+Low"}> Zhen Lin Low
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Notes+on+homotopical+algebra"} Notes on homotopical algebra
          %p A quick introduction to the topic is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"}> André Joyal
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A+crash+course+in+topos+theory+--+The+big+picture"} A crash course in topos theory – The big picture
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/747/"} Topos à l’IHES
          %p
            On
            = succeed "-toposes" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+object+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} internal to
            other
            = succeed "-toposes;" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Louis+Martini"}> Louis Martini
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sebastian+Wolf"} Sebastian Wolf
              %em Internal higher topos theory
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.06437"}> arXiv:2303.06437
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#giraudrezklurie_axioms Giraud-Rezk-Lurie axioms
          %p
            A discussion of the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+colimits"} universal colimits
            in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            presentations is due to
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Rezk"}> Charles Rezk
              ,
              %em Fibrations and homotopy colimits of simplicial sheaves
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.uiuc.edu/~rezk/rezk-sharp-maps.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            More on this with an eye on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+%E2%88%9E-bundles"} associated ∞-bundles
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthias+Wendt"}> Matthias Wendt
              ,
              %em Classifying spaces and fibrations of simplicial sheaves
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1009.2930"}> arXiv
              )
          %h3#homotopy_type_theory Homotopy type theory
          %p
            Proof that all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stack"} ∞-stack
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            have
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presentations
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
            which interpret (provide
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence"} univalent
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+universes"} type universes
          %ul
            %li#Shulman19
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Shulman"}> Michael Shulman
              ,
              %em
                All
                = succeed "-toposes" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1904.07004"}> arXiv:1904.07004
              ).
        .revisedby
